# Java Engineering Handbook

Reference: `content/java-engineering/collections-decision-matrix.md`, `content/java-engineering/jvm-flags-and-tuning.md`

## Audience

Senior engineers and **architects** — quick revision, production decisions, interview probes. **Not** a beginner tutorial.

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `data/java_engineering_modules.yaml` | 11 modules, **35 topics** (basics clubbed) |
| `data/java_engineering_order.yaml` | Flat prev/next nav |
| `scripts/build_java_engineering_handbook.py` | Regenerate all pages + prune orphans |
| `content/java-engineering/<slug>.md` | One cheat sheet per topic |

URL: `/java-engineering/<slug>/`

## Page Format (`cheatSheet: true`)

1. **At a Glance** — 3–5 bullets
2. **Reference Tables** — main content (decision matrices, Big-O, flags)
3. **Snippets** — minimal Java only when it saves time
4. **Internals & Gotchas**
5. **Production Notes**
6. **Interview Probes** — `{{< interview-answer >}}` (2–3 max)
7. **See Also**

**Do not** split primitives, wrappers, operators into separate pages — keep in `core-java-quick-ref`.

## Out of Scope

Spring Boot, Hibernate, Maven, design patterns, DSA → other handbook sections.

## Regenerate

```bash
python scripts/build_java_engineering_handbook.py
```

Edits to page bodies live in `PAGE_BODIES` inside the build script unless you hand-edit markdown (hand edits overwritten on regen).
